il communications with the current and incoming students regarding required documentation and processing. The office hours for this position will be Monday through Friday between the hours of 7AM- 3PM Assist in the daily operations of Student Health Services in support of Sick Call/ medical appointments and scheduling. Collect, maintain, and transmit as required, U.S.C.G., SUNY and State and Federally required medical documentation required for current, incoming, and former students as required by records retention policies. Manage and maintain phone and email contacts with Student Health Services for both campus departments and outside entities Responsible for record maintenance ensuring records are up to date in Pyramid Perform other duties as assigned. Requirements: Required Qualifications Associate's degree 2-5 years of Microsoft office experience. Possess a working knowledge of computer applications and web-based technologies Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree Additional Information: Classification/Salary Range : The Staff Assistant/Office Manager is a UUP position. The anticipated salary range for the position is $51,261 - $55,000 annually, with an outstanding benefits package (for more information please see the Full-Time UUP Benefits Summary). Salary will be commensurate with experience and qualifications. Review of applications to commence immediately and conclude when the position is filled. Special Notes: This is a full-time calendar year temporary appointment UUP Position.  Fair Labor Standard Acts (FLSA) Exempt position, not eligible for the overtime provisions of the FLSA.  Internal and external search to occur simultaneously. Budget Title: Staff Assistant Local Title: Office Manager Line #: 00171 SUNY Maritime College is an Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disabled/Affirmative Action employer, committed to recruiting, supporting and fostering a diverse community of outstanding faculty, staff and students. All qualified applicants will receive consi