    "https://maritime.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204352": {
      "title": "Student Engagement and Advising Center Advisor",
      "description": "SUNY Maritime College\nJob Posting: Student Engagement and Advising Center Advisor SUNY Maritime College \n\tJob Posting: Student Engagement and Advising Center Advisor Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Student Engagement and Advising Center Advisor Category: Administrative & Professional Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Academic Affairs Locations: Bronx, NY Posted: Sep 3, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $60,000.00 - $60,000.00 Position ID: 204352 Share About SUNY Maritime College: SUNY Maritime College located on a 55-acre scenic waterfront property on the outskirts of New York City on the Throggs Neck peninsula where the East River meets Long Island Sound. The campus blends the best of two worlds: a comfortable college-town feel with the greatest city in the world. An impressive view of the sound extends toward the North Atlantic, yet only a few miles away are Yankee Stadium and midtown Manhattan. SUNY Maritime offers an array of employment opportunities stemming from entry level to professional positions which encourage growth and development among its employees. Job Description: The SUNY Reconnect & Adult Learner Advisor at SUNY Maritime College reports to the Director of the Student Engagement and Advising Center (SEA Center) and serves as the College's single designated point of contact for the SUNY Reconnect program, a SUNY System initiative that helps adult learners with some college credit but no credential return to complete a degree. The Advisor manages a caseload of prospective and enrolled Reconnect students and other adult learners, coordinating outreach, admissions, program planning, and credit-for-prior-learning evaluation, and ensuring the College meets SUNY Central's reporting and compliance requirements for the program. This position also contributes more broadly to advising capacity within the SEA Center, supporting adult learners and current students outside of traditional daytime hours. Core Responsibilities: Serve as the College's single point of contact for prospective and enrolled Reconnect students, liaising with Admissions and the Registrar's Office to ensure award eligibility is identified and integrated into the admissions process consistent with SUNY guidance. Conduct proactive outreach to prospective adult learners, coordinating with the SUNY Recruitment Response Center and NYS Department of Labor Career Center referrals, and supporting recruitment efforts using SUNY's Reconnect campaign kits and campus-specific materials. Develop and maintain program maps for the AAS program so adult learners have a clear, credit-efficient path to completion, including winter/summer term sequencing. In coordination with the College Registrar, identify and process credit for prior learning, including prior military, technical, or maritime industry experience. Hold regular evening/weekend advising hours aligned with adult learners' schedules, and coordinate wraparound supports (tutoring referrals, career advising, non-academic guidance) so students are not routed through multiple offices. Track program participation and outcomes and prepare the reporting SUNY Central requires of participating campuses. Work with the Director of the SEA Center and the Assistant Director of the SEA Center on early alert management and accommodations testing support. Represent the program and department on appropriate committees and at campus recruitment and student-success events. Other duties as assigned. Requirements: Required Qualifications: Bachelor's degree required; Master's-level education preferred (can be working towards degree). Minimum 1 year of experience in academic advising, admissions, enrollment management, or related student services; experience serving adult or nontraditional learners preferred. Knowledge of degree/program requirements, transfer articulation, and credit-for-prior-learning evaluation processes. General knowledge of individual advising and counseling techniques and the principles of individual and group behavior. Ability to analyze complex situations accurately and adopt effective courses of action. Ability to carry out a variety of professionally complex assignments without detailed instructions and to manage a caseload independently. Strong interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to build relationships with prospective and current students, faculty, and campus offices. Willingness and ability to work regular evening and occasional weekend hours to accommodate adult learners' schedules. Proficiency in utilizing computer, student information systems, and word processing software. Research shows that women and people from underrepresented groups often apply to jobs only if they meet 100% of the qualifications. We recognize that it is highly unlikely that someone meets 100% of the qualifications for a role. If much of this job description describes you, then please apply for this role. Additional Information: Classification/Salary Range : The Student Engagement and Advising Center Advisor is a UUP position. The anticipated salary range for the position is $60,000 annually, with an outstanding benefits package (for more information please see the Full-Time UUP Benefits Summary . Salary will commensurate with experience and qualifications. Review of applications to commence immediately and conclude when the position is filled. Special Notes: This is a full-time calendar year appointment UUP Position.  Fair Labor Standard Acts (FLSA) Exempt position, not eligible for the overtime provisions of the FLSA.  Internal and external search to occur simultaneously. Budget Title: Staff Assistant Local Title: Student Engagement and Advising Center Advisor Line #: 00343 SUNY Maritime College is an Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disabled/Affirmative Action employer, committed to recruiting, supporting and fostering a diverse community of outstanding faculty, staff and students. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, or protected veteran status and will not be discriminated against on the basis of disability. For our full non-discrimination statement, see: http://www.sunymaritime.edu/affirmative-action . SUNY Maritime College is committed to maintaining a safe environment for its students, faculty, staff, volunteers and the general public that use our facilities. Therefore, in order to ensure the hiring of employees of the highest integrity and to maintain a safe campus community, SUNY Maritime College will conduct pre-employment background investigations on all individuals for whom employment is to be offered. Pursuant to Executive Order 161 , no State entity, as defined by the Executive Order, is permitted to ask, or mandate, in any form, that an applicant for employment provide his or her current compensation, or any prior compensation history, until such time as the applicant is extended a conditional offer of employment with compensation. If such information has been requested from you before such time, please contact the Office of Employee Relations at (518) 474-6988 or via email at info@goer.ny.gov . In accordance with the Title II Crime Awareness and Security Act, a copy of our crime statistics is available upon request by calling (718) 409-7305. It can also be viewed online by selecting University Police > Safety Information > Clery Safety Report (Annual Security & File Safety). Application Instructions: Persons interested in the above position should apply online. Please submit: Cover letter Resume/CV Statement addressing how past and/or potential contributions to diversity, equity, and inclusion will advance Maritime's commitment to inclusive excellence Names and contact information of three professional references Returning Applicants - Login to your SUNY Maritime Careers Account to check your completed application, check/edit your profile or to upload additional documents. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Maritime College 6 Pennyfield Avenue, Bronx, NY 10465"
